tations, recycling, and disposal operations. In addition, the company markets various materials, including fibers, such as corrugated cardboard and newsprint, plastics, glass, ferrous, and aluminum metals. Casella Waste Systems, Inc. was founded in 1975 and is headquartered in Rutland, Vermont.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Edmond R. Coletta | President, CEO & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5K people. Revenue per employee of $328K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers, improving at 11%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $15K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Casella Waste Systems, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $6.3B market cap on $1.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +19% over the past three years and +13% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 4% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $85M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 41.90\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","Accruals are elevated at -9.7% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 1.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 132% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.3234376532351564},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $3.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Growing faster than most Industrials peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is Casella Waste Systems (CWST) Cheap After Jana's Push And Earnings Optimism?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/